1
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:27,540
- Really?
- Really.

2
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:28,960
Look! That's her!

3
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:31,920
Kannawa from the Publicity Department!

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,960
The poster she proposed
won an advertising award.

5
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:55,500
THERE IN A FLASH! PLUMBER

6
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:03,000
PUBLICITY DPT - KOSUKE HITA

7
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:06,130
Okay!

8
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:07,960
Good morning.

9
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:12,290
PUBLICITY DPT - MINORI TAMANA & RIN SUZUGAYA
- Good morning.

10
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:14,540
PUBLICITY DPT - MIHARU SATO
- Good morning.

11
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:16,830
PUBLICITY DPT - MISAKI TANAKA
- Good morning.

12
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:18,830
Morning!

13
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:21,170
Good morning.

14
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:23,210
PUBLICITY DPT - KAORU HISAYAMA
- Morning, everyone!

15
00:01:23,290 --> 00:01:25,250
PUBLICITY DPT - KAORU HISAYAMA
- Good morning.

16
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:27,580
Good morning.

17
00:01:34,130 --> 00:01:35,290
Kannawa-san...

18
00:01:35,710 --> 00:01:38,460
About SQ's web announcement...

19
00:01:38,750 --> 00:01:42,960
We can no longer hire "Tsuru-san,"
the influencer we booked.

20
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,960
PUBLICITY DPT - AZUSA KANNAWA
- What should we do?

21
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:47,290
PUBLICITY DPT - AZUSA KANNAWA
- You're the one in charge of this.

22
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:51,170
PUBLICITY DPT - AZUSA KANNAWA
- Before coming to me with questions,
isn't it on you to prepare a proposal?

23
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:53,210
Y-Yes.

24
00:01:53,290 --> 00:01:55,790
If we need a stand-in, use your
available resources to find one.

25
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:58,920
Tell the other party we'll contact
them by the end of the day.

26
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,960
Th-Thank you so much.

27
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,580
Oh, man...

28
00:02:02,670 --> 00:02:05,710
I've corrected the necessary
documents to send to Planning.

29
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:08,540
- What?!
- Whoa, you did?

30
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:10,420
Thank you so much.

31
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:14,290
How do you expect to get any work
done with your desk in that state?

32
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:16,670
- Clean it up.
- Yes, ma'am!

33
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:19,170
Kannawa-san.

34
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:22,080
- Can I speak with you?
- Yes.

35
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:24,920
Kannawa-san is as cool as ever today.

36
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,080
I think you mean "scary."

37
00:02:27,170 --> 00:02:31,630
She's not wrong, but there are
nicer ways of saying things.

38
00:02:31,710 --> 00:02:33,830
PUBLICITY DPT HEAD - EIJI KUROKAWA
- As I told you a while ago,

39
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:37,040
PUBLICITY DPT HEAD - EIJI KUROKAWA
- a newbie is joining our department as of today.

40
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:44,790
- Yes.
- I'd like to put you in charge of training him.

41
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,830
Me?

42
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:51,830
Look, I understand that
you've got your hands full.

43
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:54,380
But this new kid's exceptional.

44
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:57,790
Just between you and me,
he was the top scorer on the exam!

45
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,080
I see...

46
00:02:59,170 --> 00:03:01,880
Which is why we want you,
the Publicity Department's ace,

47
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:04,250
to whip him into shape!

48
00:03:04,670 --> 00:03:05,790
I understand.

49
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,500
We had him look over the
new hire training materials,

50
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:10,960
and he was able to absorb everything so well.

51
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:13,170
And his responses were so lively...

52
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:16,540
<i>I really don't wanna!</i>

53
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:18,750
<i>Why's it gotta be me, of all people?</i>

54
00:03:18,830 --> 00:03:20,380
<i>My communication skills ain't good.</i>

55
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:23,630
<i>Surely the boss realizes</i>
<i>I don't fit in at the office...</i>

56
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,540
<i>Guess not.</i>

57
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:28,130
<i>For better or for worse, he can be so dense.</i>

58
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:31,670
<i>I finally established myself as</i>
<i>"the one who refuses to go out drinking,</i>

59
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:33,580
<i>so don't bother inviting her."</i>

60
00:03:33,670 --> 00:03:34,960
Kannawa-san?

61
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,670
Forget it. She never joins us.

62
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:39,710
<i>Things were finally getting easier.</i>

63
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:46,330
<i>Teaching the newbie how to do his job</i>
<i>isn't the only thing I'll have to do.</i>

64
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:48,170
Good morning!

65
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:51,960
Oh, Kamegawa-kun.

66
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,920
I'm sorry for arriving late!

67
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,670
I was cleaning up my probationary desk.

68
00:03:57,330 --> 00:03:59,710
Oh, sorry. Did I interrupt?

69
00:03:59,790 --> 00:04:03,960
Kamegawa-kun, this here
is your mentor, Kannawa-san.

70
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:07,040
NEW RECRUIT - YU KAMEGAWA
- It's nice to meet you! I'm Yu Kamegawa!

71
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:10,040
NEW RECRUIT - YU KAMEGAWA
- Yeah... Oh, I'm sorry!

72
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:13,290
I only need to use my surname
in these instances, right?

73
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:16,500
I'm Azusa Kannawa. It's nice to meet you.

74
00:04:16,790 --> 00:04:20,290
Yes! I'll be in your care, Kannawa-senpai!

75
00:04:20,790 --> 00:04:22,960
I expect great things of you, Kamegawa-kun!

76
00:04:23,290 --> 00:04:24,790
<i>What a good kid.</i>

77
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:28,710
- Well, I'll leave the rest to you, Kannawa-san.
- <i>He's got this friendly charm to him.</i>

78
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,750
Yes, sir.

79
00:04:31,210 --> 00:04:35,250
<i>So I'll be in charge of taking this young man,</i>
<i>new to the industry, under my wing.</i>

80
00:04:35,330 --> 00:04:38,080
<i>It's a heavy task, but I gotta do my best.</i>

81
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:46,130
MY AWKWARD SENPAI

82
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:16,080
EPISODE 1: ME? THE MENTOR?!
- "Me? The Mentor?!"

83
00:06:19,330 --> 00:06:23,630
I'm sure you heard plenty about our
company during new-employee training.

84
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:27,460
Though we started out
developing video games,

85
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:32,330
nowadays we've expanded into books,
apparel, real estate, and more.

86
00:06:33,130 --> 00:06:36,750
That means there are many more projects
for the Publicity Department to handle.

87
00:06:37,170 --> 00:06:39,460
If anything is unclear,
talk to me immediately.

88
00:06:39,540 --> 00:06:41,170
Yes, ma'am!

89
00:06:41,250 --> 00:06:42,790
My desk is here.

90
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:44,960
- And yours is next to mine.
- Yes, ma'am!

91
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:49,210
- This is the kitchen. Bring your own cup.
- Yes, ma'am!

92
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:51,630
- The copy machine.
- Yes, ma'am!

93
00:06:51,710 --> 00:06:53,880
- Behind me is the printing paper.
- Y-Yes!

94
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:58,170
- The nearest bathroom!
- Y-Yes, ma'am!

95
00:06:58,250 --> 00:06:59,500
SWEET POTATO PIE

96
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:02,960
Snacks from business trips are stashed here.

97
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,960
You're free to take whatever you want.

98
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:06,830
Th-Thank you.

99
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:09,460
I guess that covers everything.

100
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:12,170
Other places I need to show him are...

101
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:17,170
Thank you so much for giving me a tour.

102
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:20,330
Can I ask you if there's anything
I need help with?

103
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:22,210
Yes. Please do so.

104
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:26,960
<i>All right. I think I was able to</i>
<i>teach him the important stuff.</i>

105
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:33,000
- Um, Senpai...
- What is it?

106
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:35,460
Oh, excuse me, but...

107
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:38,460
I was wondering what I'm
supposed to do for today.

108
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:43,920
<i>I needed to teach him how to do his job!</i>

109
00:07:45,670 --> 00:07:48,380
I'm about to go to a meeting with a client.

110
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:50,670
I'll have you join me.

111
00:07:50,750 --> 00:07:52,330
U-Understood!

112
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:55,540
You only need to shadow me
and observe the meeting.

113
00:07:55,630 --> 00:07:57,000
But before that...

114
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:02,750
- Let's practice exchanging business cards.
- Yes, ma'am.

115
00:08:02,830 --> 00:08:06,170
You don't need to focus too hard
on business manners,

116
00:08:06,250 --> 00:08:09,330
but you should make it a habit
to get used to the basics—

117
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,710
Here you go, Senpai.

118
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:38,710
Please allow our newcomer
to join the meeting today.

119
00:08:39,710 --> 00:08:42,790
I'm Kamegawa. It's nice to meet you all.

120
00:08:43,210 --> 00:08:45,630
Nice to meet you, Kamegawa-san.

121
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,790
<i>A refreshing greeting...</i>

122
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:50,380
AZUSA KANNAWA
- <i>A smooth business card exchange...</i>

123
00:08:50,710 --> 00:08:54,040
<i>Whereas I, the mentor,</i>
<i>exchanged my cards with the floor...</i>

124
00:08:54,130 --> 00:08:55,960
Based on the research shown,

125
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:59,080
we would like to disseminate
the information on social media.

126
00:08:59,170 --> 00:09:03,630
<i>I need to at least maintain my dignity</i>
<i>as a mentor while I'm working.</i>

127
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:07,290
<i>I appreciate him looking at me so sincerely,</i>

128
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:10,130
<i>but I'm getting nervous</i>
<i>from him staring so much...</i>

129
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:18,130
<i>No. Every move I make as a mentor</i>
<i>affects the new recruit's development!</i>

130
00:09:18,210 --> 00:09:20,250
<i>This is no time to be nervous!</i>

131
00:09:21,330 --> 00:09:24,960
<i>It's no use! I'm so nervous!</i>

132
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:34,290
- Good work in there, Kannawa-senpai.
- Yeah...

133
00:09:34,630 --> 00:09:35,920
<i>I'm tired.</i>

134
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:40,250
<i>Not from work, but from the</i>
<i>heavy burden of being a mentor.</i>

135
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:42,830
<i>It's almost time for lunch.</i>

136
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:46,290
<i>As his mentor, I'm the one who needs</i>
<i>to extend the invitation, right?</i>

137
00:09:48,290 --> 00:09:51,130
<i>The family restaurant I often</i>
<i>went to with Senpai could work.</i>

138
00:09:55,540 --> 00:09:59,830
<i>Isn't it considered workplace harassment for</i>
<i>a senior to ask their junior out to lunch?</i>

139
00:10:00,130 --> 00:10:01,630
<i>But if I don't invite him,</i>

140
00:10:01,710 --> 00:10:05,500
<i>it's like I'm sending the message of "I don't</i>
<i>plan on getting friendly with you," right?</i>

141
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:08,790
<i>What'll we even talk about?</i>

142
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,170
<i>The weather?</i>

143
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:11,460
<i>Stocks?</i>

144
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:16,580
<i>Daily conversations are</i>
<i>the toughest topic fer me!</i>

145
00:10:16,670 --> 00:10:17,830
Senpai?

146
00:10:18,630 --> 00:10:21,540
I! I'm going to a meeting now!

147
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:25,380
So have your lunch while I do that.

148
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:28,420
U-Understood.

149
00:10:40,330 --> 00:10:43,380
<i>What was I thinking, running away?</i>

150
00:10:55,210 --> 00:10:58,710
- I'll be heading out now.
- 'Kay.

151
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:04,170
<i>"'Kay"? Just "'kay"?</i>

152
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:07,080
<i>I could have said a word</i>
<i>of appreciation or two.</i>

153
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,330
Thank you for today.

154
00:11:09,630 --> 00:11:12,580
I'm not sure if I did well since I was so
nervous, it being my first day and all...

155
00:11:18,290 --> 00:11:21,630
No newbie is perfect
their first day on the job.

156
00:11:22,290 --> 00:11:23,960
I suppose not.

157
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:26,380
You can rely on me going forward.

158
00:11:26,460 --> 00:11:29,380
- That's what mentors are for.
- Yes, ma'am!

159
00:11:29,790 --> 00:11:32,830
I look forward to working with you
tomorrow as well, Kannawa-senpai!

160
00:11:35,210 --> 00:11:36,920
'Kay.

161
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:43,040
Good work!

162
00:11:43,130 --> 00:11:44,290
Good work today!

163
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:45,670
How did it go?

164
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:48,710
I was nervous, but thanks to
everyone, I think I managed.

165
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:55,790
He was nervous?

166
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,130
Of course he was.

167
00:11:57,210 --> 00:11:59,170
Even if he's the top scorer,
he's still a newbie.

168
00:12:00,750 --> 00:12:02,750
I'm no good.

169
00:12:02,830 --> 00:12:04,920
All I did was worry about myself.

170
00:12:06,710 --> 00:12:09,290
I need to be a reliable senpai.

171
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:14,130
For starters, I need to
be more frank with him.

172
00:12:20,250 --> 00:12:24,210
Hey, Kamegawa-kun.
What prefecture are you from?

173
00:12:24,290 --> 00:12:25,830
I'm from Saitama.

174
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:28,630
What? Me, too! Where in Saitama?

175
00:12:28,710 --> 00:12:30,250
- Over in Kawaguchi—
- Hey!

176
00:12:35,750 --> 00:12:37,710
You're in the way. Move.

177
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,330
I'm sorry!

178
00:12:50,250 --> 00:12:53,500
<i>I did it! I greeted them properly!</i>

179
00:12:57,500 --> 00:13:01,580
Today, I'll have you write up a proposal
for a small company's manga app.

180
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:02,880
Yes, ma'am.

181
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:06,210
I've prepared samples of my
past work proposals for you.

182
00:13:06,670 --> 00:13:08,330
You can use those for reference.

183
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:10,580
Yes, ma'am. Thank you so much.

184
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:14,330
<i>Just you wait.</i>

185
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:18,380
<i>Today'll be the day I invite you to lunch!</i>

186
00:13:22,830 --> 00:13:24,710
Um, Kannawa-senpai?

187
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:26,330
What?

188
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:30,170
I sent you my proposal in the work chat.
Would you look it over for me?

189
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:37,290
It's too wordy. Keep your concepts
concise and easy to understand.

190
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:39,630
Yes, ma'am. I'll fix it right away.

191
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:43,250
- You can do that after lunch.
- Yes, ma'am.

192
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:53,580
<i>This is it! This feels so natural!</i>

193
00:13:53,670 --> 00:13:55,880
<i>Okay, now's my chance!</i>

194
00:13:58,790 --> 00:14:00,630
Huh?

195
00:14:02,460 --> 00:14:04,250
Whoopsy-daisy.

196
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,500
Hot, hot, hot...

197
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:11,630
Kannawa-senpai?

198
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:15,210
You think that's adequate?

199
00:14:15,290 --> 00:14:17,670
Minding your health is also part of the job!

200
00:14:17,750 --> 00:14:20,080
You're right. I'm sorry!

201
00:14:20,170 --> 00:14:21,920
I'm on a budget, so...

202
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,170
I-Is that so?

203
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,920
<i>I totally missed the timing.</i>

204
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,630
<i>On top of that, he's broke...</i>
<i>Reduced to eatin' a single cup of ramen...</i>

205
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:34,040
<i>He's got me worryin' about him!</i>

206
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:49,210
How can a senior foster their juniors
if they can't even invite them to lunch?

207
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,920
Kanna.

208
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,540
What are you sighing about?

209
00:14:57,380 --> 00:14:58,960
It's going to be fine.

210
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:00,420
You're doing your best.

211
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:04,580
Being straightforward is your strong suit.

212
00:15:04,670 --> 00:15:07,460
I'm sure everyone will see that someday.

213
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:09,580
I guarantee it.

214
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,000
Kanzaki-senpai...

215
00:15:16,330 --> 00:15:18,330
KANKAIJI

216
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:35,290
Understood. I'll explain that
to the other party.

217
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:36,960
<i>You're a lifesaver!</i>

218
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:39,880
<i>Goes to show that what one</i>
<i>really needs is a reliable colleague!</i>

219
00:15:40,210 --> 00:15:41,630
Was that all you had to say?

220
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:45,710
<i>You should try small talk sometime.</i>

221
00:15:46,130 --> 00:15:47,290
<i>Oh, I know!</i>

222
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:51,250
<i>That collab café we worked on?</i>
<i>There's gonna be a second installment.</i>

223
00:15:51,330 --> 00:15:53,790
<i>I think you'll be hearing back</i>
<i>about work there soon.</i>

224
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:54,960
I see.

225
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:57,460
<i>Something on your mind?</i>

226
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:02,210
Just that this might be a good opportunity
to try out the new recruit.

227
00:16:02,290 --> 00:16:03,380
Yeah!

228
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:06,080
Oh, you're his mentor, right?

229
00:16:06,170 --> 00:16:09,290
To think that someone like Kannawa,
who was trained by Kanzaki-senpai,

230
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:11,580
would be the next to train others.

231
00:16:12,330 --> 00:16:14,880
What do you mean, "someone like"?

232
00:16:15,170 --> 00:16:17,880
<i>Don't be too harsh on the newbie.</i>

233
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:20,250
<i>And be sure to communicate with him.</i>

234
00:16:20,330 --> 00:16:21,630
It's no problem.

235
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:25,630
<i>I was able to greet him today,</i>
<i>and I tried to invite him to lunch!</i>

236
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:31,130
<i>For your information, "'kay" and "yeah" aren't</i>
<i>proper conversations. You know that, right?</i>

237
00:16:31,790 --> 00:16:32,750
Of course I do!

238
00:16:32,830 --> 00:16:35,210
I'm worried.

239
00:16:35,290 --> 00:16:38,960
You know how often people
change jobs nowadays, right?

240
00:16:39,330 --> 00:16:40,580
<i>Change jobs?!</i>

241
00:16:40,670 --> 00:16:43,960
<i>He's right. That's possible.</i>

242
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:46,670
<i>Oh! How about you try reading</i>
<i>self-improvement books?</i>

243
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:47,750
<i>You know, stuff like,</i>

244
00:16:47,830 --> 00:16:52,330
A MUST-READ FOR MANAGERS! A CAPABLE BOSS
- <i>"A capable boss doesn't</i>
<i>scold their subordinates!"</i>

245
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:55,130
No need.

246
00:16:55,580 --> 00:16:59,750
Other people's success stories
won't necessarily be helpful to me.

247
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,250
Good work today.

248
00:17:48,750 --> 00:17:51,670
Oh! I forgot to buy dinner!

249
00:18:02,250 --> 00:18:05,580
And after I told him that minding
your health is part of the job...

250
00:18:05,670 --> 00:18:08,460
BOOM! VEGGIES
- Veggies, check.

251
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:13,960
A CAPABLE BOSS

252
00:18:15,670 --> 00:18:19,460
"Communication skills to be the best boss."

253
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:22,080
"Greetings are fundamental to communication."

254
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:24,500
"Smile brightly."

255
00:18:25,460 --> 00:18:27,170
You're in the way. Move.

256
00:18:27,250 --> 00:18:28,960
Move.

257
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:35,380
G-Good morning, Kamegawa!

258
00:18:37,710 --> 00:18:39,040
Scary!

259
00:18:39,130 --> 00:18:42,580
If I greeted him like that,
he'd think something was up!

260
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:45,500
<i>"Communicating with your</i>
<i>subordinates in a strict tone is outdated."</i>

261
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:48,580
<i>"Instead, for them to grow, praise your</i>
<i>subordinates over and over again..."</i>

262
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:51,080
<i>"Correct them when they</i>
<i>need to be corrected..."</i>

263
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,460
Huh?

264
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:58,580
So when exactly do I praise him?
Or correct him?

265
00:19:00,670 --> 00:19:04,170
Proactive communication
increases productivity...

266
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:08,380
You can't communicate with subordinates
over drinks in this day and age...

267
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:13,080
What am I supposed to do?

268
00:19:13,170 --> 00:19:16,630
I never thought I'd have to
pay the price for giving up on

269
00:19:16,710 --> 00:19:19,540
smoothly communicating
with people like this.

270
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:25,880
Oh, no! My noodles are overdone!

271
00:19:37,540 --> 00:19:39,790
BOOM! VEGGIES

272
00:19:44,460 --> 00:19:45,540
Shoot!

273
00:19:47,540 --> 00:20:09,210
- All set!
- A mentor being late? Unbelievable!

274
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:18,960
<i>I only crammed for one night...</i>

275
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:21,540
<i>But all I can do is take it one step at a time.</i>

276
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:23,960
Getting used to the job?

277
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,330
- Yes, just a bit...
<i>- Greet with a smile.</i>

278
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:28,210
- Oh! Senpai!
- <i>Greet with a smile.</i>

279
00:20:28,290 --> 00:20:29,380
G-Good—

280
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:31,540
Kannawa-san's his mentor?

281
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:34,040
I feel sorry for that newcomer.

282
00:20:34,130 --> 00:20:35,500
She can be strict.

283
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:40,710
GENERAL AFFAIRS - AKEMI HAMAWAKI
- She always looks angry, so she's scary.

284
00:20:40,790 --> 00:20:45,580
Well, I think she gets away with it
because she's good at her job.

285
00:20:45,670 --> 00:20:49,710
What? But it's difficult to work with her.

286
00:20:51,210 --> 00:20:55,080
INTERACTING WITH YOUR JR: -GREET WITH BRIGHT SMILE!
-EXPLAIN SIMPLY! -AVOID HARSH LANGUAGE!

287
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:57,880
Oh, no! Are you all right, Senpai?

288
00:20:58,380 --> 00:21:02,170
I'm glad she wasn't my mentor.

289
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:03,540
Um...

290
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:07,250
Oh, sorry.

291
00:21:14,710 --> 00:21:17,460
Sorry. It's almost time to start the day.

292
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:25,670
- Let's go.
- I'm glad!

293
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:29,540
I get to know Kannawa-senpai's kinder side.

294
00:21:29,630 --> 00:21:31,670
I feel a bit luckier than most!

295
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:35,880
I-Is that so?

296
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:38,210
Oh, no. Kannawa-san's here.

297
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:44,460
Sorry, I overstepped.

298
00:21:46,170 --> 00:21:48,710
- I'm not going to thank you.
- Yes, ma'am.

299
00:21:50,830 --> 00:21:51,920
Thank you...

300
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:53,790
Huh? Did you say something?

301
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:56,710
- Nothing! Let's go!
- Yes, ma'am!

302
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:02,080
Kamegawa. For today's lunch—

303
00:22:02,170 --> 00:22:05,040
I'm having a veggie stick with it today!

304
00:22:05,750 --> 00:22:06,830
I see...

